From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] color: count a DCI-P3 red as wide gamut

BIsWideGamut() takes a red y below 0.320 as the sign of a wide-gamut
panel. DCI-P3 red is exactly (0.680, 0.320), so a panel profiled with P3
primaries is treated as narrow and the SDR gamut wideness slider only
adjusts clipping instead of mapping between Rec.709 and the native
gamut. Make the comparison inclusive.
---
 src/color_helpers.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/color_helpers.cpp b/src/color_helpers.cpp
index 752efaa..423f4a7 100644
--- a/src/color_helpers.cpp
+++ b/src/color_helpers.cpp
@@ -868,8 +868,8 @@ bool BIsIdentityLut( const lut1d_t & lut1d, const lut3d_t & lut3d, float flToler
 
 bool BIsWideGamut( const displaycolorimetry_t & nativeDisplayOutput )
 {
-    // Use red as a sentinal for a wide-gamut display
-    return ( nativeDisplayOutput.primaries.r.x > 0.650f && nativeDisplayOutput.primaries.r.y < 0.320f );
+    // Use red as a sentinal for a wide-gamut display; DCI-P3 red sits exactly on the threshold
+    return ( nativeDisplayOutput.primaries.r.x > 0.650f && nativeDisplayOutput.primaries.r.y <= 0.320f );
 }
 
 void buildSDRColorimetry( displaycolorimetry_t * pColorimetry, colormapping_t *pMapping,
